[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187534271","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4187534271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4187534271,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75mLO_","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T18:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T18:28:33Z","body":"I just now realized that we obviously still end up with stale gravity/damping values until the next frame when the overrides change on any overlapping `Area3D`, since they won't actually be updated until we call `_update_environmental_properties()` at the next simulation step.\r\n\r\nI was kinda hoping to not have to change `JoltArea3D` to propagate these changes from itself to all of its overlapping bodies, since that involves doing `RID` lookups for every single overlapping object when the relevant properties change, since we can't reasonably store the `JoltObject3D` reference for the overlaps (since they can go stale).\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, we're obviously now paying for the overhead of `_update_environmental_properties()` for every awake body at every single simulation step, which could be seen as being much worse, and which we could avoid if we only did this when `JoltArea3D` told us to.\r\n\r\nThoughts?\r\n\r\nEDIT: Also, just to be clear, Godot Physics has only been updating gravity/damping during the simulation step since forever basically, so this PR already puts us at parity as-is.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187534271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188107827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4188107827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4188107827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75oXQz","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T02:14:22Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T02:14:22Z","body":"> which we could avoid if we only did this when `JoltArea3D` told us to.\r\n\r\nI was curious to see what this would look like, so I've just pushed a separate commit that changes all the relevant `JoltArea3D` setters to cause `_update_environmental_properties()` to run for all its overlapping bodies. I'll admit it wasn't nearly as messy as I had imagined it.\r\n\r\nA couple of things to note though:\r\n\r\n1. I realized we can choose between a `RID` lookup and a `JPH::BodyID` lookup when iterating the area's overlaps, so I went with the latter, since that seemed less costly to me.\r\n2. We can't actually avoid calling `_update_environmental_properties()` during the simulation step in all cases, since point gravity needs up-to-date positions.\r\n3. If we're dealing with a body that has thousands of area overlaps, which in turn have thousands of overlapping objects itself, all these `JoltArea3D` setters are anything but trivial now, which bothers me a bit.\r\n4. `JoltArea3D::bodies_by_id` should absolutely be an [`AHashMap`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ee713ccb7cbaddf59f8258ed6663461779d00856/core/templates/a_hash_map.h#L46-L48) now, rather than a [`HashMap`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ee713ccb7cbaddf59f8258ed6663461779d00856/core/templates/hash_map.h#L48-L50), but I want to do a pass on the collections used in `modules/jolt_physics` in general, with some hard numbers to go along with it, so I'll leave that for later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188107827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189078365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4189078365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4189078365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75sENd","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T15:42:26Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T15:42:26Z","body":"(This last push was just to squash the two commits.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189078365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4194069783","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4194069783","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4194069783,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75_G0X","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-06T18:07:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-06T18:07:19Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4194069783/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202538199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4202538199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4202538199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76faTX","user":{"login":"greenfox1505","id":1642297,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDIyOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1642297?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505","html_url":"https://github.com/greenfox1505","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T22:19:02Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T22:19:49Z","body":"This commit 64cf02362aa38322b520341625aa1cc1b9b45881 broke rigid bodies in my project. Gravity is not being applied correctly. Reverting it \"fixes\" gravity. Not sure why yet.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202538199/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202675356","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4202675356","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4202675356,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76f7yc","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T22:53:04Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T22:53:04Z","body":"Yeah, I just found the problem. It was the removal of `_areas_changed()` in `JoltBody3D::_space_changed()` that broke it, as it never actually initializes gravity/damping unless the body is overlapping with an `Area3D`.\r\n\r\nThat was sloppy of me. It was a bit of a last minute change, and I was testing with `Area3D` gravity overrides so much that I forgot to test bodies outside of an `Area3D`. 🤦‍♂️\r\n\r\nI've put up a fix here: #118291\r\n\r\nThanks for letting us know!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202675356/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202755034","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4202755034","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4202755034,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76gPPa","user":{"login":"greenfox1505","id":1642297,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDIyOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1642297?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505","html_url":"https://github.com/greenfox1505","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T23:17:16Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:19:52Z","body":"I was digging through diffs to see what changed, but it looks like you beat me to it.\r\n\r\nI had just figured out it doesn't repro if there an area with a zero force gravity","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202755034/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4696004149","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4696004149","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4696004149,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF-dWNQ","user":{"login":"macduy","id":70455,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNDU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70455?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy","html_url":"https://github.com/macduy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macduy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-12T22:38:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T22:39:03Z","body":"Hi, I've ran into an issue and wanted to understand if this could have been brought on by this change.\r\n\r\nI have a project where I dynamically change gravity, as follows:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPhysicsServer3D.AreaSetParam(GetWorld3D().Space, PhysicsServer3D.AreaParameter.GravityVector, targetGravity);\r\n```\r\n\r\nand then recursively wake each rigid body in the scene to respond to this new gravity direction\r\n\r\n```\r\nprivate void WakeAllRigidBodies(Node node)\r\n    {\r\n        foreach (Node child in node.GetChildren())\r\n        {\r\n            if (child is RigidBody3D rigidBody)\r\n            {\r\n                GD.Print(\"Waking rigid body: \", rigidBody.Name);\r\n                rigidBody.Sleeping = false;\r\n            }\r\n            WakeAllRigidBodies(child); // Recursively check all children\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works in `4.7-dev3` but stops working in `4.7-dev4` in weird ways. I'm printing in `_IntegrateForces` of the impacted RigidBody and getting the following behaviour:\r\n- Either objects don't follow the new gravity, printing the project's default gravity or\r\n- At some point, the total gravity is `(0, 0, 0)`\r\n- Sometimes, eventually the gravity switches to the correct, desired gravity\r\n\r\nI wasn't able to determine yet what causes which behaviour.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4696004149/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4697798437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118197#issuecomment-4697798437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118197","id":4697798437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGAK3JQ","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-13T06:55:10Z","updated_at":"2026-06-13T06:55:10Z","body":"@macduy It does sound like this PR might be related to what you're describing, yes.\n\nCould I ask you to create a new issue and attach a minimal reproduction project to it? That way we can more easily verify the issue and make sure we're fixing the right thing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4697798437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]